CO2Fix_3_1

32	# simulation lenght [yr]

comments
{
Special parametrisation: coppice system of Eugalyptus globulus in Galicia, Spain, two rotations.
Mart-Jan Schelhaas
November 2004.

Data for first rotation based on 
Valero, E. and Picos, J. In prep. Biomass and carbon storage of galician Eucalyptus plantations. Field results  vs CO2Fix Model output. Submitted to Forest Ecology and Management
and
Valero, E. and Picos, J. (2002) Estudio de la Influencia de la Selvicultura en la Fijación de CO2 de un Eucaliptal tipo en Galicia mediante el modelo CO2fix. Catedra Ence. University of Vigo. Unedited

Two scenarios are present. The first scenario ("above and products") is meant for the simulation of the aboveground parts and the products. Also the roots and the soil are simulated well, but only until the moment of coppicing. After coppicing in year 16, the increment will be higher, because the root system is still intact. Relative changes in increment in second rotation are derived from yield table of A. Fernandez Lopez 1982. Relative allocation patterns to foliage and branches are assumed not to change, since no information was present here. 

The second scenario ("below and soil 1") contains the simulation of the root system and the soil after the first harvest until the second year of harvest. The initial situation for root and soils is derived from  year 16 of the first scenario, and increment and aboveground allocation are the same as for the period 16-32 in the other scenario. The allocation to the roots is assumed to change so that there is only a slight increase in total root biomass over the second rotation. This is purely hypothetical and not based on data. 

For each further coppicing event, a new scenario should be added, initialised with the stocks at the end of the previous rotation.

If the user is only interested in the results of biomass and soil, the easiest is to take the results of each scenario (1 harvest cycle) and put them in the rigth sequence. However, if the products are also of interest, they should be derived from one simulation (see first scenario), because product stocks cannot be initialised. The same is valid for the bioenergy module.
}

2	# number of Scenarios

0	# mitigation scenario
0	# baseline scenario

0	# Project duration
